# PDP AI development standards

## Mandatory reads

- **Any code change** → skim `docs/DEVELOPMENT-STANDARDS.md`
- **Architecture / new file** → `docs/ARCHITECTURE-GUIDELINES.md`
- **Review prep** → `docs/CODE-REVIEW-STANDARDS.md`

## Task → doc (+ skill / command)

| Task | Doc | Skill / command |
|------|-----|-----------------|
| Gemini API, prompt, retries | `docs/features/gemini-llm.md`, `docs/API-INTEGRATION.md` | skill `change-gemini-prompt`; rule `gemini-prompt-changes.mdc` |
| Messages / injection | `docs/features/message-passing.md` | — |
| DOM apply | `docs/features/dom-updates.md` | — |
| Popup / options UI | `docs/features/popup-ui.md`, `docs/features/options-api-key.md` | — |
| Manual validation | `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md` | skill `manual-test-pdp`; command `test-extension` |
| Debug production-like issues | `docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md`, `docs/playbooks/debug-extension.md` | skill `debug-chrome-extension` |
| Release | `docs/playbooks/release-extension.md` | — |

## Non-negotiable

- Minimize scope; match existing Angular / TypeScript patterns under `projects/` and `libs/`
- Run `npm run build:extension` before manual Chrome validation
- Never commit or log Gemini API keys or full PDP HTML
- Update matching `docs/features/*.md` when behavior in that feature changes
- Prefer amending existing docs over new doc files
